[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140973819","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109172#issuecomment-3140973819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109172","id":3140973819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67N3T7","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T18:37:09Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T18:46:02Z","body":"I'll admit that this looks a bit strange at first glance, since I doubt anyone will ever actually use `print_raw` from the engine code, like we do with `print_line` and such, but the other options were either to have a bespoke reentrance guard in `VariantUtilityFunctions::printraw`, which would mean you could technically recurse once from `Logger._log_message`, or to move the reentrance guards to `core/os/os.cpp`, which would mean `print_handler_list` would not be covered at all instead.\r\n\r\nIf anyone has a better idea, I'm all ears.\r\n\r\nEDIT: I guess just exposing/sharing the `thread_local bool` somehow is another possibility, but that starts to feel a bit messy.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140973819/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148509825","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109172#issuecomment-3148509825","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109172","id":3148509825,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67qnKB","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-03T15:54:03Z","updated_at":"2025-08-03T15:54:03Z","body":"Probably, but that's more 4.6 territory in scope; this solution doesn't change anything exposed, so rolling it back with proper protections should be straightforward","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148509825/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148533892","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109172#issuecomment-3148533892","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109172","id":3148533892,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67qtCE","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-03T16:28:08Z","updated_at":"2025-08-03T16:28:08Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3148533892/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3149716548","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109172#issuecomment-3149716548","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109172","id":3149716548,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67vNxE","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T08:59:15Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T08:59:15Z","body":"> Shouldn't we protect `OS::print` (and sibling) functions instead?\r\n\r\nThat was my thinking as well, but again, certain error handlers (like `EditorLog`) are only invoked through `print_handler_list` found in `print_string.cpp`, and not when calling `OS::print*`, so you effectively have two entry points for printing.\r\n\r\nSeeing as how `OS::print*` is not directly callable through the bindings, and sparsely used throughout the engine in general, it seemed like covering `print_string.cpp` was more important. This does mean that you can technically get in trouble from things like custom modules if you use `OS::print*` in a `Logger`, but scripts and extensions should be fully covered (I hope).\r\n\r\nObviously we could just add another reentrance guard to `OS::print*` as well, or share one somehow. Perhaps that's justified, I don't know.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3149716548/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3149732949","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109172#issuecomment-3149732949","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109172","id":3149732949,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67vRxV","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T09:04:48Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T09:04:48Z","body":"Well, I was mostly thinking because all `printraw` does is call `OS::print`, so any guards implemented in `OS::print` would perfectly safeguard `printraw` as well. Making `printraw` effectively just a glue function; the effective binding for `OS::print`. Not sure why it was designed this way in the first place.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3149732949/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3149924416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109172#issuecomment-3149924416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109172","id":3149924416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67wAhA","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T10:05:19Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T10:05:19Z","body":"> so any guards implemented in `OS::print` would perfectly safeguard `printraw` as well\r\n\r\nRight, for `printraw` specifically it works to have it only be guarded in `os.cpp`, but if you have a bespoke guard for only that function then you're subject to single recursion weirdness, like being able to recurse once from `Logger._log_message` if it was called due to `print_rich` or something.\r\n\r\nHaving it cover all the print functions in `os.cpp` would obviously solve that problem, but you'd still need the guard in `print_string.cpp` as well, to cover `print_handler_list`.\r\n\r\n> Not sure why it was designed this way in the first place.\r\n\r\nI'm mostly curious as to why `print_handler_list` and `error_handler_list` exist outside of `OS`, instead of being invoked as part of `OS::print*` and `OS::printerr*`. That would simplify things a bit.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3149924416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]